{
  "schema": 1,
  "updated": "2026-09-12",
  "note": "Commands offered when binding a key from the keyboard view. Every one is either bound by CS2 itself in game/csgo/cfg/user_keys_default.vcfg, or already listed in cs2cfg/cfgscan.py as an engine command or engine action -- so nothing here is a guess about what the engine accepts. A command that does not exist would bind silently and then do nothing when pressed, which is the failure this list exists to avoid.",
  "sources": [
    "CS2's own cfg/user_keys_default.vcfg, read at runtime by cs2cfg/defaults.py",
    "KNOWN_ENGINE_COMMANDS and KNOWN_ENGINE_ACTIONS in cs2cfg/cfgscan.py"
  ],
  "hold_note": "A command written with a leading + is held, not tapped: the engine runs the + form while the key is down and the matching - form when it is released. Binding one is normal and needs no matching -bind.",
